[center][color=#ff0000][size=6][b]OFFLINE ONLY[/b][/size][/color][/center]
[size=4][b]This mod is UNOFFICIAL![/b][/size]
[size=4]It is not affiliated with the ERR team, the Convergence Team, or any other overhaul authors, and they don't support this mod.[/size]
[size=4][color=#ff0000]Do [b]NOT[/b][/color] ask for help in the official ERR, Convergence or any other discord channels while this mod is installed. Remove it first, then check whether your problem is still there.[/size]
[size=5][color=#ff0000]I am not responsible if you get kicked or banned.[/color][/size]
[size=4]For questions and bug reports - join the [/size][size=6][url=https://discord.gg/JvTMwPCygB][b]Discord server[/b][/url][/size]

[size=5][b]Compatible with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/510]Seamless Co-op[/url][/b][/size]

[center][b][color=#ec6d13][size=6]DESCRIPTION[/size][/color][/b]
[color=#ff8c00][size=4]DLL version[/size][/color] of the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/3091][size=4]Map for Goblins[/size][/url] mod.
Thousands of loot and world icons on the in-game map, and [b]no regulation.bin changes[/b].[/center]

This mod supports many overhauls, pick the one for your game:
[list]
[*][b]Vanilla version[/b], for the base game + Shadow of the Erdtree (not required). ~7400 icons. Also works with the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/428]Item & Enemy Randomizer[/url] - see details below.[/*]
[*][b]ERR version[/b], for the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/541]ERR[/url]. ~9700 icons, including the ERR-specific stuff (Rune Pieces, Ember Pieces, Kindling Spirits, unique loot etc).[/*]
[*][b]Convergence version[/b], for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/3419]The Convergence[/url] (3.x, me3), ~8700 icons. The mod includes the new/relocated loot, new bosses and reworked zones.[/*]
[*][b]ERTE version[/b], for the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/2747]ERTE[/url], ~8800 icons.[/*]
[*][b]Golden Age version[/b], for the [url=https://afdian.com/a/moke16864]Elden Ring Golden Age[/url] overhaul (me3), ~7500 icons.[/*]
[*][b]ELDEN VINS version[/b], for the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/4709]ELDEN VINS[/url] overhaul (me3), ~8000 icons.[/*]
[*][b]Elden Ring Reborn version[/b], for the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/2202]Elden Ring Reborn[/url] overhaul (me3), ~7500 icons.[/*]
[*][b]Graceborne version[/b], for the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/5207]Graceborne[/url] Bloodborne-inspired overhaul (me3), ~7400 icons.[/*]
[*][b]DM Throne version[/b], for the [url=https://www.patreon.com/cw/puyuan]Dark Moon: Throne[/url] overhaul (me3), ~7500 icons.[/*]
[/list]
[i]Each build is up to date to the game/overhaul version it was generated from. After a major update to that game or overhaul, I will update this mod.[/i]

[size=5][color=#ff8c00][b]Install as any other DLL mod[/b][/color][/size]
This is a pure DLL mod: the only files are [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] (config file). All icon categories are [b]ON by default[/b] - open the ini, or press [b][color=#ff8c00]F10[/color][/b] (or [b][color=#ff8c00]Y+R3[/color][/b] on a controller) in-game, to turn off any you don't want.
[b]Updating from an older version?[/b] Just replace the DLL file with the new one.


[center][b][color=#ec6d13][size=6]IN-GAME MOD MENU[/size][/color][/b][/center]
[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/10062/10062-1789662788-1434295795.png[/img][/center]
Press [b][color=#ff8c00]F10[/color][/b] (keyboard) or [b][color=#ff8c00]Y+R3[/color][/b] (controller) to open the mod menu inside the game. There you can:
[list]
[*]Turn any icon category on or off (or use [b]Show all[/b] / [b]Hide all[/b])[/*]
[*]Track your completion on the [color=#ec6d13][b]Progress[/b][/color] tab: collected/total per region (grouped into The Lands Between, the Underground and Shadow of the Erdtree), and click a category to highlight only its uncollected markers right on the map[/*]
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/10062/10062-1789663806-45288346.png[/img]
[*]Hide individual markers you don't care about, and bring them back, from the [color=#ec6d13][b]Hidden[/b][/color] tab[/*]
[*]Search any known item by its name from the [color=#ec6d13][b]Search[/b][/color] tab[/*]
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/10062/10062-1789663533-1858092352.png[/img]
[*]Flip the master "Show map icons" switch[/*]
[*]Change the mod's settings from the [color=#ec6d13][b]Settings[/b][/color] page - map fragment requirement, killed-boss, spoiler-free mode etc[/*]
[*]Copy a marker dump for bug reports[/*]
[/list]
[b]Toggling a category takes effect immediately[/b] - its icons appear or disappear without closing the map. Some other options, such as spoiler-free mode, apply the next time you open the map, you don't need to restart the game. Mouse, keyboard and controller supported.

[color=#ec6d13][size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][b]In-game [color=#ec6d13]mod menu[/color][/b] (see above): [color=#ec6d13]F10[/color] (or [color=#ec6d13]Y+R3[/color] on a controller) opens a settings panel to toggle icon categories, the master switch and Show all / Hide all without editing the ini. Category toggles take effect right away on the open map.[/*]
[*]Icon [color=#ec6d13]categories[/color] that can be turned on/off individually: weapons, armour, talismans, spells, key items, smithing stones, gloveworts, cookbooks, bell bearings, gathering nodes, bosses, graces, stakes of Marika, spirit springs, imp statues, paintings, summoning pools, map fragments, gestures, NPC invaders, puzzles etc.[/*]
[*]Icons in a region only show up after you've found that region's map fragment (can be disabled).[/*]
[*]Things you've already collected disappear from the map: including gathered [color=#ec6d13]material nodes[/color] (like Arteria Leaf), Rune/Ember Pieces etc. Defeated bosses either hide or get a checkmark (configurable).[/*]
[*][color=#ec6d13][b]Progress tracking[/b][/color]: the [b]Progress[/b] tab shows how much of each category you've collected per region (grouped into The Lands Between, the Underground and Shadow of the Erdtree, with small caves/catacombs folded into their region). Click a category to light up only its uncollected markers on the open map.[/*]
[*][color=#ec6d13][b]Items Search[/b][/color]: use the [b]Search[/b] tab to find and highlight any item by name (merchant stock is not included).[/*]
[*][b][color=#ec6d13]Hide markers[/color] you don't want[/b]: hover a marker on the world map and press [color=#ec6d13][b]Delete[/b][/color] (or [color=#ec6d13][b]RB[/b][/color] on a controller) to hide the icon. The [color=#ec6d13][b]Hidden[/b][/color] tab lists your hidden markers so you can restore them. Hidden markers persist and are saved per character.[/*]
[*]Hovering a marker on the map shows a [color=#ec6d13][b]small tooltip[/b][/color] with the info how far above or below you it is.[/*]
[*][b][color=#ec6d13]Focus [/color]for markers at your current location[/b]: markers of the map you are on are drawn bigger and brighter, markers of another map smaller and dimmer. Can be configured in the mod menu.[/*]
[*][b]Live marker [color=#ec6d13]deoverlapping[/color][/b]: overlapping icons are spread apart using only the markers visible at that moment, so a category you turn off frees its space.[/*]
[*]Every marker shows its location name, down to sub-areas (like Siofra Aqueduct/Siofra River etc). The mod uses original game strings, everything should be [color=#ec6d13]localised[/color] out of the box.[/*]
[*]The INI maintains itself. If there's no file - it gets created. If there are new options after an update - they will be added automatically.[/*]
[*]Master on/off for all icons at the top of the menu, or [color=#ec6d13][b]F10[/b][/color] / [color=#ec6d13][b]Y+R3[/b][/color] directly when the menu is turned off in the ini.[/*]
[*][b]Item & Enemy [color=#ec6d13]Randomizer[/color] support[/b] (vanilla build, on by default): loot markers read the loaded regulation at startup, so each one shows the item that's [i]actually[/i] there - right name, right icon - and disappears when you pick up the real light point. Works with any seed, no per-seed setup. Turn it off in the ini if you play vanilla without the randomizer.[/*]
[*][color=#ec6d13][b]Spoiler-free mode[/b][/color] (optional, set anonymous_loot in the ini): every loot marker shows a plain "?" icon and a generic label instead of the real item, so you can find loot without knowing what it is - made for blind / randomizer runs.[/*]
[/list]


[center][b][color=#ec6d13][size=6]HOW TO INSTALL[/size][/color][/b][/center]
[color=#ec6d13][size=4][b]Vanilla version[/b][/size][/color]
[b]Option A: ModEngine3 (me3)[/b]
[spoiler][list=1]
[*]Install me3 ([url=https://github.com/garyttierney/me3/releases]me3_installer.exe[/url], docs at [url=https://me3.help/]me3.help[/url])[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] next to your .me3 profile (e.g. eldenring-default.me3)[/*]
[*]Open the [b][color=#ec6d13].me3[/color][/b] profile in Notepad and add a new [color=#f2995a][[natives]][/color] section:
[code]profileVersion = "v1"

[[supports]]
game = "eldenring"

[[natives]]
path = 'MapForGoblins.dll'[/code][/*]
[*]Double-click the .me3 file to play[/*]
[/list][/spoiler]
[b]Option B: ModEngine2[/b]
[spoiler][list=1]
[*]Get [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]ModEngine2[/url] and extract it anywhere ([color=#ff0000]NOT[/color] into the game folder)[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into the ModEngine2 directory (next to launchmod_eldenring.bat)[/*]
[*]In [b][color=#ec6d13]config_eldenring.toml[/color][/b], under [modengine], add [color=#f2995a]"MapForGoblins.dll"[/color] to the [color=#f2995a]external_dlls[/color] parameter:
[code]external_dlls = [ "MapForGoblins.dll" ][/code][/*]
[*]Run launchmod_eldenring.bat[/*]
[/list][/spoiler]
[b]Option C: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url][/b] [i](simple DLL loader)[/i]
[spoiler]This mod is a plain DLL, so it loads through Elden Mod Loader like any other DLL mod.
[list=1]
[*]Install Elden Mod Loader (by techieW): extract its files into your [b]Game[/b] folder (next to eldenring.exe) - it adds dinput8.dll, mod_loader_config.ini and a [b]mods[/b] folder[/*]
[*][b]Open [color=#ec6d13][b]mod_loader_config.ini[/b][/color] and set [color=#ff0000]load_delay = 0[/color][/b][/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into that [b]mods[/b] folder (EML loads every DLL in there at startup)[/*]
[*]Launch the game [b][color=#f2995a]offline[/color][/b] (EML does not bypass EAC, so play [color=#f2995a]offline[/color])[/*]
[/list][/spoiler]
[b]Option D: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/5998]Mod Engine 2 with Lazy Loader[/url][/b]
[spoiler]Same as ModEngine2, but its config lives in the [b]base/[/b] folder.
[list=1]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into the main [b]Game[/b] folder (next to eldenring.exe)[/*]
[*]Open [b][color=#ec6d13]base/config.toml[/color][/b] and add the DLL to [color=#f2995a]external_dlls[/color]:
[code]external_dlls = [
"MapForGoblins.dll"
][/code][/*]
[*]Launch from eldenring.exe[/*]
[/list]
The DLL must be in [b]external_dlls[/b]: Lazy Loader only loads ModEngine from base/, it does not auto-inject mod DLLs.[/spoiler]

[size=4][b]Using it with the [color=#ec6d13]Item & Enemy Randomizer[/color][/b][/size]
Use the [b]Vanilla version[/b]. Install it the same way (ModEngine3/me3 or ModEngine2), alongside the randomizer's generated [b]regulation.bin[/b] in your load order. Nothing else to set up: the live-loot options are [b]on by default[/b] in the vanilla build, so at startup the markers read your loaded seed and show the real item (name + icon) and hide on the actual light-point pickup. For a blind run, set [b]anonymous_loot = true[/b] in the ini to replace every loot marker with a "?" and a generic label.

[color=#ec6d13][size=4][b]ERR version[/b][/size][/color]
[spoiler][list=1]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into your ERR [color=#ec6d13][b]dll\offline\[/b][/color] folder[/*]
[*]Launch the ERR via [color=#ec6d13][b]OFFLINE[/b][/color] launcher[/*]
[/list][/spoiler]

[color=#ec6d13][size=4][b]Convergence version[/b][/size][/color] (3.x, me3)
[spoiler]Convergence 3.x launches through a [b].me3[/b] profile in ConvergenceER\me3 (convergence.me3, and convergence - seamless.me3 if you use Seamless Co-op).
[list=1]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into [color=#ec6d13][b]...\ConvergenceER\mod\dll[/b][/color] (next to ErdTools.dll, erdyes.dll, etc.)[/*]
[*]Open the [b][color=#ec6d13].me3[/color][/b] profile you launch with in Notepad and add a new [color=#f2995a][[natives]][/color] section:
[code][[natives]]
path = './../mod/dll/MapForGoblins.dll'[/code][/*]
[*]Launch the game through Start_Convergence.bat[/*]
[/list][/spoiler]

[color=#ec6d13][size=4][b]ERTE version[/b][/size][/color]
[spoiler]ERTE runs on [b]Mod Engine 3 (me3)[/b] through its .me3 profile (e.g. eldenring-ERTE-SOTE-CoopReady.me3).
[list=1]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into a "MapForGoblins" folder next to ERTE's mod folder, i.e. into [color=#ec6d13][b]...\me3\config\profiles\eldenring-mods\MapForGoblins\[/b][/color] (alongside the "ERTE SOTE" folder)[/*]
[*]Open the ERTE [color=#ec6d13][b].me3[/b][/color] profile file in any text editor and add a new [color=#f2995a][[natives]][/color] section:
[code][[natives]]
path = 'eldenring-mods\MapForGoblins\MapForGoblins.dll'[/code][/*]
[*]Launch through the ERTE .me3 profile[/*]
[/list][/spoiler]

[color=#ec6d13][size=4][b]Golden Age[/b][/size][/color] (me3)
[spoiler]Golden Age ships its own [b]Mod Engine 3[/b] and launches through [b]Start_GoldenAge.me3[/b] (or Start_GoldenAge.bat).
[list=1]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into the Golden Age folder (next to Start_GoldenAge.bat and Start_GoldenAge.me3)[/*]
[*]Open [color=#ec6d13][b]Start_GoldenAge.me3[/b][/color] in a text editor and add the DLL to the natives list (one more line inside the existing [b][color=#f2995a]natives [/color]= [ ... ][/b] block):
[code]natives = [
...existing entries...,
{ path = "MapForGoblins.dll" },
][/code][/*]
[*]Launch through Start_GoldenAge.bat[/*]
[/list]
A Golden Age update replaces Start_GoldenAge.me3, so after updating the overhaul add the line again.[/spoiler]

[color=#ec6d13][size=4][b]ELDEN VINS[/b][/size][/color] (me3)
[spoiler]ELDEN VINS launches through its [b]ELDEN VINS.me3[/b] profile and serves its DLLs from [b]mod\dll[/b].
[list=1]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into [color=#ec6d13][b]...\ELDEN VINS\mod\dll\[/b][/color] (next to ErdTools.dll and Scripts-Data-Exposer-FS.dll)[/*]
[*]Open [b][color=#ec6d13]ELDEN VINS.me3[/color][/b] in a text editor and add a new [color=#f2995a][[natives]][/color] section:
[code][[natives]]
path = "mod/dll/MapForGoblins.dll"[/code][/*]
[*]Launch through [color=#ec6d13]ELDEN VINS.me3[/color][/*]
[/list]
An ELDEN VINS update replaces the .me3 profile, so after updating the overhaul add the entry again.[/spoiler]

[color=#ec6d13][size=4][b]Elden Ring Reborn[/b][/size][/color] (me3)
[spoiler]Elden Ring Reborn launches through [b]me3[/b] with its [b]RebornConfiguration.me3[/b] profile.
[list=1]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into the Reborn folder (next to RebornConfiguration.me3)[/*]
[*]Open [b][color=#ec6d13]RebornConfiguration.me3[/color][/b] in a text editor and add a new [color=#f2995a][[natives]][/color] section at the end:
[code][[natives]]
path = 'MapForGoblins.dll'[/code][/*]
[*]Launch Reborn with its launcher .bat as usual[/*]
[/list]
Reborn used to launch through ModEngine2: an external_dlls entry in config_eldenring.toml is no longer read, use the [[natives]] entry instead. If a Reborn update replaces RebornConfiguration.me3, add the entry again.[/spoiler]

[color=#ec6d13][size=4][b]Graceborne[/b][/size][/color] (me3)
[spoiler]Graceborne launches through its [b].me3[/b] profile (launch.me3) and serves the mod from its [b]mod[/b] folder.
[list=1]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into Graceborne's [b]mod[/b] folder, i.e. [b][color=#ec6d13]...\GRACEBORNE\mod\[/color][/b] (next to regulation.bin and Scripts-Data-Exposer-FS.dll)[/*]
[*]Open [b][color=#ec6d13]launch.me3[/color][/b] in a text editor and add a new [color=#f2995a][[natives]][/color] section:
[code][[natives]]
path = 'mod/MapForGoblins.dll'[/code][/*]
[*]Launch via Graceborne's .me3 launcher[/*]
[/list][/spoiler]

[color=#ec6d13][size=4][b]Dark Moon: Throne[/b][/size][/color] (me3)
[spoiler]Dark Moon: Throne launches through its own [b].me3[/b] profile (e.g. TL-ER.me3) next to its launcher .bat.
[list=1]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into the Throne folder (next to the .me3 profile and the launcher .bat)[/*]
[*]Open the [b][color=#ec6d13].me3[/color][/b] profile in a text editor and add a new [color=#f2995a][[natives]][/color] section:
[code][[natives]]
path = 'MapForGoblins.dll'[/code][/*]
[*]Launch through the Throne launcher .bat as usual[/*]
[/list]
A Throne update replaces the .me3 profile, so after updating the overhaul add the entry again.[/spoiler]


[center][b][color=#ec6d13][size=6]REQUIREMENTS[/size][/color][/b][/center]
[list]
[*]Vanilla version: a DLL loader - [url=https://github.com/garyttierney/me3/releases]ModEngine3[/url], [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]ModEngine2[/url], or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url][/*]
[*]ERR version: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/541]ERR[/url] itself, nothing else. The mod loads through ERR's own loader.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/3419]The Convergence[/url] / [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/2747]ERTE[/url] / [url=https://afdian.com/a/moke16864]Golden Age[/url] / [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/4709]ELDEN VINS[/url] / [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/5207]Graceborne[/url] / [url=https://www.patreon.com/cw/puyuan]Dark Moon: Throne[/url] versions: the matching overhaul installed (me3). Shadow of the Erdtree is required by the overhauls themselves.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/2202]Elden Ring Reborn[/url] version: an installed Elden Ring Reborn (it ships its own me3). Shadow of the Erdtree is required by the overhaul itself.[/*]
[*][color=#ff0000][b][size=4]OFFLINE ONLY.[/size][/b][/color] Mod loaders disable EAC, so the "Inappropriate activity detected" message at launch is normal.[/*]
[/list]


